{
  "cdmVersionRange": ">=5.0.0",
  "_README": [
    "Antihypertensive exposure outside an inpatient stay: the medication half of the mFI-5 hypertension item (1 point).",
    "Subramaniam 2018 (from ACS NSQIP HYPERMED) scores hypertension only when it requires medication. Added 2026-11-06 at the study team's request.",
    "ATC 2nd-level classes with descendants: C02 ANTIHYPERTENSIVES (21600381), C03 DIURETICS (21601461), C07 BETA BLOCKING AGENTS (21601664),",
    "C08 CALCIUM CHANNEL BLOCKERS (21601744), C09 AGENTS ACTING ON THE RENIN-ANGIOTENSIN SYSTEM (21601782), exactly as covariates/covariate_concepts_mfi5.csv :: htn.",
    "Diuretics and beta blockers have non-hypertensive indications; the item therefore also requires a hypertension diagnosis at any time before index",
    "(cohort 9100022), combined at score level via cohort_map.csv and_cohort_id, the same pattern as the insulin item (9100007 AND 9100021).",
    "Outpatient rule identical to 9100007: no inpatient visit (9201, 262, with descendants) spans the exposure start date; exposures with no visit link are kept.",
    "Window (set in cohort_map.csv, not here): 365 days before index, chosen 2026-11-06 over the NSQIP-literal 30 days because EHR medication lists are sparse.",
    "VERIFY: 21600381 (C02) was not observable in the synthetic characterization output; confirm it against the vocabulary before the PRCC run.",
    "PrimaryCriteriaLimit / QualifiedLimit / ExpressionLimit are all \"All\" and EndStrategy is StartDate+0, like every covariate cohort here."
  ],
